        "topic": "Metal extraction methods",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2005",
        "question_text": "<p>The process of extracting iron from its ore using a blast furnace involves the reduction of <b>haematite</b> ($Fe_2O_3$) with which of the following?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>In a blast furnace, iron is extracted from haematite ($Fe_2O_3$) by reducing it with carbon monoxide ($CO$), which is produced from the reaction of coke (carbon) with oxygen. The other options (hydrogen, nitrogen, and chlorine) are not used in this process.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
